      "decision": "pure-lane shards; protected lanes are injected post-selection as whole batches",
      "experiment": "E1",
      "finding": "In arm P the scheduler's lane tag and the actual document content agree exactly, so the delivered Indic share is auditable straight from the consumption ledger. In arm M they diverge: the ledger reports the CARRIER lane, so the protected lane's true delivery is invisible to every downstream audit that reads mixture_lanes. That is the decisive difference - not the share itself but whether the share can be measured at all. A floor you cannot audit is not a floor, and S5's own measurement of the course's always-on lane (stated 8%, delivered ~15%) is exactly what an unauditable floor looks like.",
      "floor": 0.12,
      "hypothesis_refuted": false,
      "question": "mixed-lane vs pure-lane shards for delivering a protected floor",
      "refutation_criterion": "refuted if arm M delivers the floor within +/-1pp AND its per-stage spread is no worse than arm P"
